    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 53\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 8411, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to the denial\n      of access to public records that relate to  civil  investigations;\n      to  amend  the  executive law, in relation to requiring the super-\n      intendent of state police to provide the department  of  law  with\n      direct,  real-time  access  to  the criminal gun clearinghouse; to\n      amend the executive law and the civil rights law, relating to  the\n      enforcement powers of the attorney general; to amend the education\n      law,  in  relation  to authorizing the attorney general to enforce\n      the provisions of the education law against covered  entities  who\n      engage  in  discrimination  and  the  powers  and  duties of state\n      university trustees; and  to  amend  the  public  health  law,  in\n      relation to the compromise of certain claims the state may have\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would: require the New York State Police to give Office of\nthe Attorney General (OAG) direct, real-time access to the criminal  gun\nclearinghouse;  amend the Freedom of Information Law to expand the scope\nof the law enforcement exemption from disclosure; eliminate the require-\nment that OAG approve waivers or settlements of patient bills under  the\nPublic Health Law and Education law; and expand OAG's explicit authority\nto  authorize  OAG  to bring several causes of action, including actions\nunder the Human Rights Law and Civil Rights Law for unlawful discrimina-\ntory practices, under the Executive Law for unlawful patterns  or  prac-\ntices  by  law  enforcement  agencies,  and  under the Education law for\nrepeated or persistent discrimination.\n \n  While I support the goals of several of the provisions  of  this  law,\nsuch  as  those aimed at improving certain enforcement tools and stream-\nlining  interagency  processes,  other  components  of  the  bill  raise\nconcerns, such as providing direct, real-time remote access to the crim-\ninal  gun  clearinghouse,  which raises operational concerns and creates\nfiscal issues. Each of the components of this bill deserves  independent\nconsideration,  rather  than  be  combined  in  a  single bill with many\nproposals that do not interrelate. Given that, I am constrained to  veto\nthis  bill,  though have directed my staff to consider and discuss these\nproposals with the OAG for potential future adoption, either  by  legis-\nlation or administratively.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
